{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 2849 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "07d8c8818629ba8c39170c5fa0e3aa7e0f559774c0b524bea6d13c13c08c705a" :edb/db-before-t 2848 :edb/db-after-t 2849 :edb/tx-data [[13194139536161 50 #inst "2026-10-09T17:39:50.003Z" 13194139536161 true] [17592186172062 1020 #edb/ref 17592186386649 13194139536161 true] [17592186172062 1020 #edb/ref 17592186386663 13194139536161 true] [17592186172063 1020 #edb/ref 17592186386642 13194139536161 true] [17592186172063 1020 #edb/ref 17592186386656 13194139536161 true] [17592186172308 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139536161 true] [17592186172308 1100 "$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nConsider the surface integral of the function \n$f(x,y,z)=x+y+z$ \nover the parametric surface \n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨{u}^{2},\\,u-{v}^{2},\\,{v}^{2}⟩\n$$\n\nfor $(u,v)\\in D⊆{R}^{2}.$ What is the missing expression?\n\n*Hint: You can use the fact that $‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖=2v\\sqrt{1+8{u}^{2}}.$*" 13194139536161 true] [17592186172308 1100 "$∬_(S)f(x, y, z)dS = ∬_(D)AAAAAAAdA$\nConsider the surface integral of the function\n$f(x, y, z) = x + y + z$\nover the parametric surface\n$r(u, v) = ⟨u^{2}, u - v^{2}, v^{2}⟩$\nfor $(u, v) ∈ D⊆R^{2}$. What is the missing expression?\n\n*Hint: You can use the fact that $‖r_{u}^{′} \\cdot r_{v}^{′}‖ = 2v\\sqrt{1 + 8u^{2}}$.*" 13194139536161 false] [17592186172308 1145 "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface integral of a scalar function $f$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}f(r(u,v))‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nNotice that we are told that the norm of the fundamental vector product for our surface is\n\n$$\n‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖=\\sqrt{{u}^{2}+{v}^{2}+1}.\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(u,v)) & =(x+y+z)\\,{|}_{x={u}^{2}\\,y=u-{v}^{2}\\,z={v}^{2}} \\\\  & ={u}^{2}+(u-{v}^{2})+{v}^{2} \\\\  & ={u}^{2}+u\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}f(r(u,v))‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,2({u}^{2}+u)v\\sqrt{1+8{u}^{2}}\\,\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536161 true] [17592186386642 1017 #edb/ref 17592186386643 13194139536161 true] [17592186386642 1089 "q-161127" 13194139536161 true] [17592186386642 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139536161 true] [17592186386642 1100 "Evaluate the surface integral \n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}{x}^{2}-2yz\\,\\text{d}S,\n$$\n\nwhere the parametric surface $S$ is defined by the equations\n\n$$\nx=u+v,\\,y=u,\\,z=v\n$$\n\nfor $-1\\le u\\le 1$ and $0\\le v\\le 1.$" 13194139536161 true] [17592186386642 1113 #uuid "18dc2b17-918c-58cb-b73a-247a9dacca45" 13194139536161 true] [17592186386642 1145 "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface integral of a scalar function $f$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}f(r(u,v))‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn vector form, our surface has the equation \n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u+v,\\,u,\\,v⟩.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u+v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,1,\\,0⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u+v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,-1,\\,-1⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖ & =‖⟨1,\\,-1,\\,-1⟩‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+-{1}^{2}+-{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+1+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(u,v)) & ={x}^{2}-2yz\\,{|}_{x=u+v\\,y=u\\,z=v} \\\\  & =(u+v)^{2}-2uv \\\\  & ={u}^{2}+{v}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, if we denote \n\n$$\nD={(u,v)\\,:\\,-1\\le u\\le 1,\\,0\\le v\\le 1},\n$$\n\nour surface integral can be written as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}{x}^{2}-2yz\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}f(r(u,v))‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,({u}^{2}+{v}^{2})\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}{∬}_{D}\\,{u}^{2}+{v}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}({\\int }_{-1}^{1}{u}^{2}+{v}^{2}\\,\\text{d}u)\\text{d}v \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{[\\frac{{u}^{3}}{3}+u{v}^{2}]}_{u=-1}^{u=1}\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{2}{3}+2{v}^{2}\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}{[\\frac{2}{3}v+\\frac{2}{3}{v}^{3}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}(\\frac{2}{3}+\\frac{2}{3})-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536161 true] [17592186386643 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386644 13194139536161 true] [17592186386643 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386645 13194139536161 true] [17592186386643 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386646 13194139536161 true] [17592186386643 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386647 13194139536161 true] [17592186386643 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386648 13194139536161 true] [17592186386643 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536161 true] [17592186386643 1041 "selection" 13194139536161 true] [17592186386643 1104 #edb/ref 17592186386644 13194139536161 true] [17592186386643 1110 #uuid "2aca348c-b9d8-59de-9e27-7a16826b1f7d" 13194139536161 true] [17592186386644 1034 "\\frac{4\\sqrt{3}}{3}" 13194139536161 true] [17592186386644 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536161 true] [17592186386644 1111 #uuid "6dc79d0a-8c51-580f-a70e-03efc7799663" 13194139536161 true] [17592186386645 1034 "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3}" 13194139536161 true] [17592186386645 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536161 true] [17592186386645 1111 #uuid "26aa5890-8eea-56e1-bb15-1ae9d870ebb2" 13194139536161 true] [17592186386646 1034 "2" 13194139536161 true] [17592186386646 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536161 true] [17592186386646 1111 #uuid "405ab8f8-79dd-58fa-bf1e-c63cc69f4824" 13194139536161 true] [17592186386647 1034 "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}" 13194139536161 true] [17592186386647 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536161 true] [17592186386647 1111 #uuid "f0c444b7-89a7-5cc0-84ed-a2a363a5d2da" 13194139536161 true] [17592186386648 1034 "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}" 13194139536161 true] [17592186386648 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536161 true] [17592186386648 1111 #uuid "7c1d2d62-ef56-51e9-a12e-36f44901e7e2" 13194139536161 true] [17592186386649 1017 #edb/ref 17592186386650 13194139536161 true] [17592186386649 1089 "q-161132" 13194139536161 true] [17592186386649 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139536161 true] [17592186386649 1100 "$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nConsider the surface integral of the function \n$f(x,y,z)=xy+z$ \nover the parametric surface \n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u,\\,{u}^{2},\\,2v⟩\n$$\n\nfor $(u,v)\\in D⊆{R}^{2}.$ What is the missing expression?\n\n*Hint: You can use the fact that $‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖=\\sqrt{16{u}^{2}+4}$*" 13194139536161 true] [17592186386649 1113 #uuid "9de41d79-7798-5e1d-b077-c1d9dece4dd9" 13194139536161 true] [17592186386649 1145 "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface integral of a scalar function $f$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}f(r(u,v))‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nNotice that we are told that the norm of the fundamental vector product for our surface is\n\n$$\n‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖=\\sqrt{16{u}^{2}+4}.\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(u,v)) & =(xy+z)\\,{|}_{x=u\\,y={u}^{2}\\,z=2v} \\\\  & =u.{u}^{2}+2v \\\\  & ={u}^{3}+2v\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}f(r(u,v))‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,({u}^{3}+2v)\\sqrt{16{u}^{2}+4}\\,\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536161 true] [17592186386650 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386651 13194139536161 true] [17592186386650 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386652 13194139536161 true] [17592186386650 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386653 13194139536161 true] [17592186386650 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386654 13194139536161 true] [17592186386650 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386655 13194139536161 true] [17592186386650 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536161 true] [17592186386650 1041 "selection" 13194139536161 true] [17592186386650 1104 #edb/ref 17592186386655 13194139536161 true] [17592186386650 1110 #uuid "da9cec8d-74e8-52c2-ae1f-8e2db9fb815a" 13194139536161 true] [17592186386651 1034 "({u}^{3}+{v}^{3})\\sqrt{16{v}^{2}+4}" 13194139536161 true] [17592186386651 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536161 true] [17592186386651 1111 #uuid "e8da5aa1-8d0e-55ed-91ee-d844c9cdf4b1" 13194139536161 true] [17592186386652 1034 "({v}^{2}+2u)\\sqrt{16{u}^{2}+4}" 13194139536161 true] [17592186386652 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536161 true] [17592186386652 1111 #uuid "a2b16629-a7fe-5f86-b675-3f8d563a25dd" 13194139536161 true] [17592186386653 1034 "({v}^{3}+2v)\\sqrt{16{u}^{2}+4}" 13194139536161 true] [17592186386653 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536161 true] [17592186386653 1111 #uuid "ee3f3752-41e8-57cf-b880-71e4d4df98c5" 13194139536161 true] [17592186386654 1034 "(u+v)\\sqrt{16{u}^{2}+4}" 13194139536161 true] [17592186386654 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536161 true] [17592186386654 1111 #uuid "e2caf314-d7f1-59d5-9aa2-0020f0effcdb" 13194139536161 true] [17592186386655 1034 "({u}^{3}+2v)\\sqrt{16{u}^{2}+4}" 13194139536161 true] [17592186386655 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536161 true] [17592186386655 1111 #uuid "11f6382a-1260-56a0-853e-48b8938ccdb6" 13194139536161 true] [17592186386656 1017 #edb/ref 17592186386657 13194139536161 true] [17592186386656 1089 "q-161242" 13194139536161 true] [17592186386656 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139536161 true] [17592186386656 1100 "Evaluate the surface integral \n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}x(y+z)\\,\\text{d}S,\n$$\n\nwhere the parametric surface $S$ is defined by the equations\n\n$$\nx=2u,\\,y=-3v,\\,z=4v\n$$\n\nfor $0\\le u\\le 2$ and $0\\le v\\le 2.$" 13194139536161 true] [17592186386656 1113 #uuid "28d5c29f-26b0-57e9-aad1-66eedd869c86" 13194139536161 true] [17592186386656 1145 "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface integral of a scalar function $f$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}f(r(u,v))‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn vector form, our surface has the equation \n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨2u,\\,-3v,\\,4v⟩.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(2u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(-3v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(4v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,\\,0,\\,0⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(2u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(-3v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(4v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,-3,\\,4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,-8,\\,-6⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖ & =‖⟨0,\\,-8,\\,-6⟩‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+(-8)^{2}+(-6)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{0+64+36} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{100} \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(u,v)) & =x(y+z)\\,{|}_{x=2u\\,y=-3v\\,z=4v} \\\\  & =2u(-3v+4v) \\\\  & =2uv\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, if we denote \n\n$$\nD={(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 2,\\,0\\le v\\le 2},\n$$\n\nour surface integral can be written as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}x(y+z)\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}f(r(u,v))‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,2uv\\cdot 10\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =5{∬}_{D}\\,4uv\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =5{\\int }_{0}^{2}2u\\,\\text{d}u\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{2}2v\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & =5\\cdot [{u}^{2}]_{0}^{2}\\cdot [{v}^{2}]_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =5\\cdot 4\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =80.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536161 true] [17592186386657 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386658 13194139536161 true] [17592186386657 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386659 13194139536161 true] [17592186386657 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386660 13194139536161 true] [17592186386657 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386661 13194139536161 true] [17592186386657 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386662 13194139536161 true] [17592186386657 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536161 true] [17592186386657 1041 "selection" 13194139536161 true] [17592186386657 1104 #edb/ref 17592186386660 13194139536161 true] [17592186386657 1110 #uuid "9f5a4b86-941d-5ccc-bc6e-ab729cae9ce1" 13194139536161 true] [17592186386658 1034 "85" 13194139536161 true] [17592186386658 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536161 true] [17592186386658 1111 #uuid "e71a2a0e-7d8e-5f9c-96c9-d38be230e6c9" 13194139536161 true] [17592186386659 1034 "95" 13194139536161 true] [17592186386659 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536161 true] [17592186386659 1111 #uuid "4e40515d-5766-55e4-b6e4-553a2fe93566" 13194139536161 true] [17592186386660 1034 "80" 13194139536161 true] [17592186386660 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536161 true] [17592186386660 1111 #uuid "67eefd6c-